      "id": "01",
      "title": "The redirect path",
      "question": "Walk through what happens when someone clicks a short link.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "URL shortener, question one. Walk through what happens when someone clicks a short link, and which redirect status you return. Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "What happens when someone <em>clicks</em> a short link?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "A click sends a GET request for the short code to a web server. The server checks the cache first. On a hit, it has the long URL immediately. On a miss, it reads the database, then fills the cache, so the next click is a hit. Then it responds with a redirect, whose Location header carries the long URL. And if the code is not in the database at all, it returns not found.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Cache first, <em>then</em> the database",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "client",
                "label": "Browser",
                "x": 210,
                "y": 470,
                "w": 220,
                "h": 70
              },
